# Tracked content that's pure search noise: generated, vendored, or
# mirrored, never something a repo-wide grep is looking for (#437).
# .gitignore is the other half of this pair — it excludes what's
# untracked (e.g. .claude/worktrees/); this file excludes what's tracked
# but still noise, since gitignore patterns apply regardless of tracked
# status for any ripgrep-family consumer (this file, `rg`, Claude Code's
# Grep tool).

# git-cliff generated — markdownlint/prettier already skip it too (AGENTS.md).
/CHANGELOG.md

# LazyVim lockfile — machine-generated, not hand-edited.
/nvim/lazy-lock.json

# Catppuccin submodules, vendored upstream, not this repo's own content.
/theme/
